{
  "esm": "2.1.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "conservative_overlap",
    "description": "Conservative overlap-area regridding, factored as a template library (esm-spec 9.7) so a coupling can invoke it instead of restating the aggregates inline. This is the library form of exactly the computation in the ESS worked fixtures tests/valid/geometry/conservative_regrid_overlap_join.esm and tests/coupling/cross_domain_coupling.esm (esm-spec 8.6 / 8.6.1): F_tgt[j] = (1/A_j) * sum_i A_ij * F_src[i], with A_ij = the overlap area of src_i and tgt_j (the esm:std/geometry.esm templates overlap_area_planar / overlap_area_spherical, esm 2.0.0) and A_j = sum_i A_ij. The match-less templates factor the stages: (1) conservative_overlap_A_ij_planar / conservative_overlap_A_ij_spherical -- the NARROW PHASE as a dense evaluable faq whose element is the scalar overlap-area template of esm:std/geometry.esm (esm-spec 8.6.1: the template returns the scalar area with its convex clip written out in its body, so the narrow phase is a dense tensor contraction with no ragged clip-ring intermediate); (2) conservative_overlap_A_j -- the ROW-NORMALIZATION denominator, the group-by-j row-sum of the SAME computed areas with the sliver filter A_ij > atol (CONFORMANCE_SPEC 5.8.2), which is what makes partition-of-unity sum_i W_ij = 1 EXACT BY CONSTRUCTION (5.8.3: the denominator is the row-sum of the computed areas, not the true target-cell area) -- note the denominator applies the SAME filter as the numerator, so the surviving sets coincide and the invariant is exact; (3) conservative_overlap_apply -- the weighted-sum APPLY + NORMALIZE, F_tgt[j] = sum_i A_ij*F_src[i] / A_j[j] over the same filtered set (the sparse mat-vec of ConservativeRegridding.jl, W_ij = A_ij/A_j folded in). THE BROAD PHASE IS THE SPATIAL-OVERLAP JOIN GATE (projection-pushdown Phase 2a): (4) the _gated narrow-phase/assembly variants (conservative_overlap_A_ij_gated_planar / _A_j_gated / _W_ij_gated / _apply_gated) -- the SAME aggregates with the candidate join folded in as a join.overlap{src_env:[src_poly], tgt_env:[tgt_poly]} gate. The engine builds the candidate (i,j) set ONCE at build time from the cell-ring ENVELOPES -- each ring's axis-aligned bounding box, derived by the engine from the SAME polygon stacks the narrow phase clips (no hand-authored binning coordinate, no bin key, no bin-width parameter), inflated outward by a small eps -- byte-identically in every binding. A product term is contributed only where the source and target envelopes intersect (src_poly is the QUERY side, tgt_poly the INDEXED cell side), so the contraction runs over O(#candidates) instead of O(NSRC*NTGT). DENSE OR GATED IS THE CONSUMER'S CHOICE, value-identically: with the sliver filter present the two forms agree EXACTLY -- a non-candidate pair has disjoint bounding boxes hence zero true overlap area, which the dense path computes and the filter drops while the gated path never visits it; identical surviving sets, identical sums, and adding exact-zero terms to a nonnegative-area sum is FP-exact. The broad phase is ADMISSIBLE BY CONSTRUCTION: envelope candidacy never misses a genuine positive-area overlap for any eps >= 0 (two cells whose interiors overlap have overlapping bounding boxes), so no consumer bin-width admissibility obligation remains -- disjoint cell clusters are still pruned automatically (their bounding boxes do not intersect). The gated A_j applies the SAME join gate AND the SAME filter as the gated numerator, so the surviving sets coincide and partition-of-unity stays exact by construction -- the denominator broad-phases like the numerator. Cell polygons ARRIVE AS TEMPLATE PARAMETERS (closed vertex rings shaped [cells, overlap_cell_verts, overlap_coord], CCW, ring vertex v = [lon, lat]), so the templates are grid-agnostic: any pair of grids that can present its cells as fixed-vertex-count rings flows through unchanged (regridding/cartesian_cell_rings.esm derives such rings from a uniform cartesian grid spec; grids/mpas/grid.esm's mpas_cell_rings_deg derives them from MPAS mesh vertex data). Grid sizes are load-time metaparameters (NSRC, NTGT source/target cell counts; NVERT ring length, default quads), bound at the import edge; the defaults match the 3x3 -> 2x2 conformance exemplar. The MANIFOLD is chosen by WHICH narrow-phase template a consumer applies (esm 2.0.0 removed the polygon_intersection_area leaf and its manifold field; esm-spec 4.2 'Removed ops'): conservative_overlap_A_ij_planar clips in the source/target coordinate plane (areas in the squared coordinate unit; exact for the lon-lat-rectangle coarsening exemplar and for any projected patch), and conservative_overlap_A_ij_spherical clips with great-circle edges on the unit sphere (areas in steradians; the correct model for lat-lon-on-sphere regridding, with the CONFORMANCE_SPEC 5.8.4 great-circle-edge caveat for parallel edges). All three narrow-phase templates are the same pairwise skeleton (conservative_overlap_pairs, or conservative_overlap_pairs_gated with the broad-phase join) around a per-manifold element (conservative_overlap_area_planar_ij / conservative_overlap_area_spherical_ij). The spherical template reads [cells, verts, overlap_xyz] UNIT-VECTOR stacks, which the consumer builds from its lon-lat rings with conservative_overlap_unit_rings (a faq of esm:std/geometry.esm lonlat_to_unit over the ring's own cell and vertex axes); the planar templates read the lon-lat (or projected x-y) rings directly. Both take the source and target ring slot counts (src_nv, tgt_nv) explicitly, since a ring stack's vertex axis need not be overlap_cell_verts (an MPAS source ring is padded to maxEdges); a consumer binds them to the same metaparameter that sizes that axis, so the count is stated once. The broad phase is planar-envelope only, so the gated variants are planar. Everything downstream of A_ij (A_j, W_ij, apply and their gated forms) is manifold-agnostic. Conformance contract for consumers: candidate set byte-identical (when the broad phase is used), conservation and partition-of-unity as the primary exact gates, per-pair areas/weights toleranced with the sliver floor (CONFORMANCE_SPEC 5.8.1-5.8.3), and dense/gated value-identity gated exactly where both paths are computed. Exemplars: tests/conformance/regridding/conservative_overlap_3x3_to_2x2/ (dense, planar), conservative_overlap_sphere_fan_4_to_2/ (dense, spherical), conservative_overlap_gated_3x3_to_2x2/ (gated vs dense value-identity on the exemplar geometry), conservative_overlap_gated_clusters_4_to_2/ (gated with genuine candidate pruning across disjoint clusters), cartesian_rings_regrid_3x3_to_2x2/ (grid-spec -> rings -> broad phase -> narrow phase -> apply, end-to-end declarative), and mpas_l0_to_octants_sphere/ (MPAS mesh-derived rings on the sphere).",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:regrid",
      "method:conservative_overlap",
      "manifold:planar",
      "manifold:spherical",
      "conservation",
      "partition-of-unity"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Jones, P. W. (1999). First- and second-order conservative remapping schemes for grids in spherical coordinates. Monthly Weather Review 127(9), 2204-2210.",
        "doi": "10.1175/1520-0493(1999)127<2204:FASOCR>2.0.CO;2"
      },
      {
        "citation": "EarthSciAST esm-spec.md 8.6/8.6.1 (regridding is a coupling expression; the overlap-area templates of esm:std/geometry.esm) and CONFORMANCE_SPEC.md 5.8 (geometry tolerance contract).",
        "notes": "The library factoring mirrors the ESS worked fixtures tests/valid/geometry/conservative_regrid_overlap_join.esm (equations 2-5) and tests/coupling/cross_domain_coupling.esm (rg_A / rg_At / heat_flux)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "metaparameters": {
    "NSRC": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 9,
      "description": "Number of source cells (the flattened source-cell enumeration the polygon ring array and F_src are shaped over). Default matches the 3x3 exemplar."
    },
    "NTGT": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 4,
      "description": "Number of target cells. Default matches the 2x2 exemplar."
    },
    "NVERT": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 4,
      "description": "Vertices per cell polygon ring (default: quadrilateral cells)."
    }
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "src_cells": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": "NSRC"
    },
    "tgt_cells": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": "NTGT"
    },
    "overlap_cell_verts": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": "NVERT"
    },
    "overlap_coord": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 2
    },
    "overlap_xyz": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 3
    }
  },
  "expression_template_imports": [
    {
      "ref": "esm:std/geometry.esm",
      "only": [
        "overlap_area_planar",
        "overlap_area_spherical",
        "lonlat_to_unit"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "expression_templates": {
    "conservative_overlap_pairs": {
      "params": [
        "src_ring",
        "tgt_ring",
        "area"
      ],
      "description": "DENSE PAIRWISE SKELETON (narrow-phase scaffold shared by the planar and spherical A_ij templates): the [src_cells, tgt_cells] matrix whose (i, j) entry is the expression bound to `area`, evaluated with loop symbols i (source cell) and j (target cell) in scope -- bind `area` to conservative_overlap_area_planar_ij or conservative_overlap_area_spherical_ij, which read exactly those symbols. src_ring and tgt_ring are the ring stacks the element gathers from (the faq's args). Every source/target pair is visited; see conservative_overlap_pairs_gated for the broad-phase-pruned form.",
      "body": {
        "op": "faq",
        "semiring": "sum_product",
        "output_idx": [
          "i",
          "j"
        ],
        "ranges": {
          "i": {
            "from": "src_cells"
          },
          "j": {
            "from": "tgt_cells"
          }
        },
        "args": [
          "src_ring",
          "tgt_ring"
        ],
        "expr": "area"
      }
    },
    "conservative_overlap_pairs_gated": {
      "params": [
        "src_ring",
        "tgt_ring",
        "area"
      ],
      "description": "GATED PAIRWISE SKELETON: conservative_overlap_pairs with the spatial-overlap broad phase folded in as a join.overlap{src_env:[src_ring], tgt_env:[tgt_ring]} gate, so `area` is evaluated only for the candidate (i, j) pairs whose ring envelopes (axis-aligned bounding boxes inflated by eps) intersect; every other entry is the additive identity 0. The envelopes are planar, so src_ring / tgt_ring are the lon-lat (or projected x-y) rings, never unit-vector stacks.",
      "body": {
        "op": "faq",
        "semiring": "sum_product",
        "output_idx": [
          "i",
          "j"
        ],
        "ranges": {
          "i": {
            "from": "src_cells"
          },
          "j": {
            "from": "tgt_cells"
          }
        },
        "join": [
          {
            "overlap": {
              "src_env": [
                "src_poly"
              ],
              "tgt_env": [
                "tgt_poly"
              ],
              "eps": 1e-09
            }
          }
        ],
        "args": [
          "src_ring",
          "tgt_ring"
        ],
        "expr": "area"
      }
    },
    "conservative_overlap_area_planar_ij": {
      "params": [
        "src_poly",
        "tgt_poly",
        "src_nv",
        "tgt_nv"
      ],
      "description": "NARROW-PHASE ELEMENT, PLANAR: the esm:std/geometry.esm overlap_area_planar of source cell i of src_poly and target cell j of tgt_poly, i.e. one entry of A_ij. It reads the loop symbols i and j of the enclosing conservative_overlap_pairs / conservative_overlap_pairs_gated faq, so it is only meaningful bound to that skeleton's `area`. src_poly and tgt_poly are [cells, verts, overlap_coord] lon-lat (or x-y) stacks; src_nv and tgt_nv are the vertex slot counts of their rings.",
      "body": {
        "op": "apply_expression_template",
        "args": [],
        "name": "overlap_area_planar",
        "bindings": {
          "ring_a": "src_poly",
          "cell_a": "i",
          "nv_a": "src_nv",
          "ring_b": "tgt_poly",
          "cell_b": "j",
          "nv_b": "tgt_nv"
        }
      }
    },
    "conservative_overlap_area_spherical_ij": {
      "params": [
        "src_unit",
        "tgt_unit",
        "src_nv",
        "tgt_nv"
      ],
      "description": "NARROW-PHASE ELEMENT, SPHERICAL: the esm:std/geometry.esm overlap_area_spherical of source cell i of src_unit and target cell j of tgt_unit, i.e. one entry of A_ij. It reads the loop symbols i and j of the enclosing conservative_overlap_pairs / conservative_overlap_pairs_gated faq, so it is only meaningful bound to that skeleton's `area`. src_unit and tgt_unit are [cells, verts, overlap_xyz] unit-vector stacks; src_nv and tgt_nv are the vertex slot counts of their rings.",
      "body": {
        "op": "apply_expression_template",
        "args": [],
        "name": "overlap_area_spherical",
        "bindings": {
          "ring_a": "src_unit",
          "cell_a": "i",
          "nv_a": "src_nv",
          "ring_b": "tgt_unit",
          "cell_b": "j",
          "nv_b": "tgt_nv"
        }
      }
    },
    "conservative_overlap_unit_rings": {
      "params": [
        "lonlat_ring",
        "ring_cells",
        "ring_verts"
      ],
      "description": "UNIT-VECTOR RING STACK (input adapter for conservative_overlap_A_ij_spherical): the [ring_cells, ring_verts, overlap_xyz] stack of unit vectors of the lon-lat-degree ring stack lonlat_ring, each entry the esm:std/geometry.esm lonlat_to_unit of one vertex component, so the trig is evaluated once per vertex rather than once per cell pair. ring_cells and ring_verts NAME the index sets lonlat_ring is shaped over (e.g. src_cells and overlap_cell_verts, or an MPAS mesh's cells and maxEdges), so one template serves source and target stacks of any grid.",
      "body": {
        "op": "faq",
        "args": [],
        "output_idx": [
          "c",
          "v",
          "d"
        ],
        "ranges": {
          "c": {
            "from": "ring_cells"
          },
          "v": {
            "from": "ring_verts"
          },
          "d": {
            "from": "overlap_xyz"
          }
        },
        "expr": {
          "op": "apply_expression_template",
          "args": [],
          "name": "lonlat_to_unit",
          "bindings": {
            "ring": "lonlat_ring",
            "cell": "c",
            "vert": "v",
            "comp": "d"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "conservative_overlap_A_ij_planar": {
      "params": [
        "src_poly",
        "tgt_poly",
        "src_nv",
        "tgt_nv"
      ],
      "description": "NARROW PHASE, PLANAR (overlap-weight template): the raw overlap-area matrix A_ij[i,j] = overlap_area_planar(src_poly[i], tgt_poly[j]) (esm:std/geometry.esm) as a dense evaluable faq (esm-spec 8.6.1): conservative_overlap_pairs over the conservative_overlap_area_planar_ij element, clipping with straight edges in the coordinate plane; areas in the squared coordinate unit. src_poly is shaped [src_cells, verts, overlap_coord], tgt_poly [tgt_cells, verts, overlap_coord]; each cell is a closed convex vertex ring with vertex v = [lon, lat] (or [x, y] on a projected patch), either orientation. src_nv is the slot count of each source ring (its vertex axis length), tgt_nv of each target ring; a ring shorter than its slot count repeats its last vertex, which contributes nothing. Bind src_nv / tgt_nv to the SAME metaparameter that sizes the ring stack's vertex axis, never to a separate literal: a count below the axis length silently clips each cell as a polygon with fewer vertices, and because the A_j denominator row-sums the same (wrong) areas, partition-of-unity and conservation still hold -- no invariant gate would catch it. Entries for disjoint pairs are exactly 0; near-tangent slivers are dropped downstream by the atol filter of the A_j / apply templates, never here -- the raw areas are what the CONFORMANCE_SPEC 5.8.2 tolerance gates compare.",
      "body": {
        "op": "apply_expression_template",
        "args": [],
        "name": "conservative_overlap_pairs",
        "bindings": {
          "src_ring": "src_poly",
          "tgt_ring": "tgt_poly",
          "area": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "conservative_overlap_area_planar_ij",
            "bindings": {
              "src_poly": "src_poly",
              "tgt_poly": "tgt_poly",
              "src_nv": "src_nv",
              "tgt_nv": "tgt_nv"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "conservative_overlap_A_ij_spherical": {
      "params": [
        "src_unit",
        "tgt_unit",
        "src_nv",
        "tgt_nv"
      ],
      "description": "NARROW PHASE, SPHERICAL (overlap-weight template): the raw overlap-area matrix A_ij[i,j] = overlap_area_spherical(src_unit[i], tgt_unit[j]) (esm:std/geometry.esm) as a dense evaluable faq (esm-spec 8.6.1): conservative_overlap_pairs over the conservative_overlap_area_spherical_ij element, clipping with great-circle edges on the unit sphere; areas in steradians (multiply by R^2 for a physical area). src_unit is shaped [src_cells, verts, overlap_xyz], tgt_unit [tgt_cells, verts, overlap_xyz]: UNIT-VECTOR ring stacks, built by the consumer from its lon-lat-degree rings with conservative_overlap_unit_rings, so the conversion is computed once per vertex rather than once per pair. src_nv is the slot count of each source ring (its vertex axis length), tgt_nv of each target ring; a ring shorter than its slot count repeats its last vertex, which contributes nothing. Bind src_nv / tgt_nv to the SAME metaparameter that sizes the ring stack's vertex axis, never to a separate literal: a count below the axis length silently clips each cell as a polygon with fewer vertices, and because the A_j denominator row-sums the same (wrong) areas, partition-of-unity and conservation still hold -- no invariant gate would catch it. Agrees with the removed polygon_intersection_area(manifold spherical) within the CONFORMANCE_SPEC 5.8.2 tolerance, not bit for bit. Entries for disjoint pairs are exactly 0; slivers are dropped downstream by the atol filter.",
      "body": {
        "op": "apply_expression_template",
        "args": [],
        "name": "conservative_overlap_pairs",
        "bindings": {
          "src_ring": "src_unit",
          "tgt_ring": "tgt_unit",
          "area": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "conservative_overlap_area_spherical_ij",
            "bindings": {
              "src_unit": "src_unit",
              "tgt_unit": "tgt_unit",
              "src_nv": "src_nv",
              "tgt_nv": "tgt_nv"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "conservative_overlap_A_j": {
      "params": [
        "A_ij",
        "atol"
      ],
      "description": "ROW NORMALIZATION (partition-of-unity template): the per-target-cell denominator A_j[j] = sum_i A_ij[i,j] over the surviving-overlap set (filter A_ij > atol -- the CONFORMANCE_SPEC 5.8.2 sliver floor; sub-atol areas are equal-to-zero and contribute the additive identity). Because the apply template divides by THIS row-sum of the SAME computed areas under the SAME filter, the weights W_ij = A_ij/A_j satisfy sum_i W_ij = 1 exactly by construction (5.8.3), regardless of edge-model or clipping error -- the exact invariant the conformance gate asserts. This is ConservativeRegridding.jl's dst_areas (row-sums of the intersections matrix), equation (3) of the ESS overlap-join fixture.",
      "body": {
        "op": "faq",
        "semiring": "sum_product",
        "output_idx": [
          "j"
        ],
        "ranges": {
          "i": {
            "from": "src_cells"
          },
          "j": {
            "from": "tgt_cells"
          }
        },
        "filter": {
          "op": ">",
          "args": [
            {
              "op": "index",
              "args": [
                "A_ij",
                "i",
                "j"
              ]
            },
            "atol"
          ]
        },
        "args": [
          "A_ij"
        ],
        "expr": {
          "op": "index",
          "args": [
            "A_ij",
            "i",
            "j"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    "conservative_overlap_W_ij": {
      "params": [
        "A_ij",
        "A_j",
        "atol"
      ],
      "description": "NORMALIZED WEIGHTS (observability template): the explicit weight matrix W_ij[i,j] = A_ij[i,j] / A_j[j] over the surviving-overlap set, under the SAME filter A_ij > atol as the A_j and apply templates (a filtered-out sliver's weight is exactly 0, the aggregate's additive identity). This is ConservativeRegridding.jl's W matrix that conservative_overlap_apply folds into its sparse mat-vec -- factored out as its own template so a conformance runner can gate the per-pair weights through the official build-time pathway (CONFORMANCE_SPEC 5.8.1-5.8.2; the EarthSciAST.jl BuildInspection setup-array surface). Because the denominator is the row-sum of the SAME computed areas under the SAME filter, sum_i W_ij = 1 exactly for every target cell with a surviving overlap (5.8.3). Bind A_j to the materialized result of conservative_overlap_A_j. W_ij is build-once diagnostic data: the apply template never reads it, so declaring it adds no work to the ODE hot path.",
      "body": {
        "op": "faq",
        "semiring": "sum_product",
        "output_idx": [
          "i",
          "j"
        ],
        "ranges": {
          "i": {
            "from": "src_cells"
          },
          "j": {
            "from": "tgt_cells"
          }
        },
        "filter": {
          "op": ">",
          "args": [
            {
              "op": "index",
              "args": [
                "A_ij",
                "i",
                "j"
              ]
            },
            "atol"
          ]
        },
        "args": [
          "A_ij",
          "A_j"
        ],
        "expr": {
          "op": "/",
          "args": [
            {
              "op": "index",
              "args": [
                "A_ij",
                "i",
                "j"
              ]
            },
            {
              "op": "index",
              "args": [
                "A_j",
                "j"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    "conservative_overlap_apply": {
      "params": [
        "A_ij",
        "A_j",
        "F_src",
        "atol"
      ],
      "description": "WEIGHTED-SUM APPLY (+ fold-in normalize): F_tgt[j] = sum_i A_ij[i,j]*F_src[i] / A_j[j] over the same filtered surviving set as the A_j template -- i.e. F_tgt = sum_i W_ij*F_src[i] with W_ij = A_ij/A_j, the sparse mat-vec apply of ConservativeRegridding.jl (equations (4)+(5) of the ESS overlap-join fixture, the heat_flux observed of cross_domain_coupling.esm). Bind A_j to the materialized result of conservative_overlap_A_j so the denominator is the row-sum of the same computed areas: that is what makes partition-of-unity exact and conservation sum_j A_j*F_tgt[j] = sum_i A_i*F_src[i] hold wherever the target tiles the source domain (CONFORMANCE_SPEC 5.8.3). For a time-varying F_src this template is the apply-many half of the build-once/apply-many split; A_ij and A_j are build-once.",
      "body": {
        "op": "faq",
        "semiring": "sum_product",
        "output_idx": [
          "j"
        ],
        "ranges": {
          "i": {
            "from": "src_cells"
          },
          "j": {
            "from": "tgt_cells"
          }
        },
        "filter": {
          "op": ">",
          "args": [
            {
              "op": "index",
              "args": [
                "A_ij",
                "i",
                "j"
              ]
            },
            "atol"
          ]
        },
        "args": [
          "A_ij",
          "A_j",
          "F_src"
        ],
        "expr": {
          "op": "/",
          "args": [
            {
              "op": "*",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "index",
                  "args": [
                    "A_ij",
                    "i",
                    "j"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "op": "index",
                  "args": [
                    "F_src",
                    "i"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "op": "index",
              "args": [
                "A_j",
                "j"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    "conservative_overlap_A_ij_gated_planar": {
      "params": [
        "src_poly",
        "tgt_poly",
        "src_nv",
        "tgt_nv"
      ],
      "description": "CANDIDATE-GATED NARROW PHASE: the overlap-area matrix of conservative_overlap_A_ij_planar with the SPATIAL-OVERLAP broad-phase candidate join folded in -- join.overlap{src_env:[src_poly], tgt_env:[tgt_poly]} (projection-pushdown Phase 2a) admits a product term only where the source cell's and target cell's envelopes intersect (each ring factor's axis-aligned bounding box, computed once at build time from the SAME polygon rings the narrow phase clips; inflated outward by eps), so one polygon clip runs per CANDIDATE pair instead of per (i,j) pair: O(#candidates) build cost. src_poly is the QUERY side (src_env), tgt_poly the INDEXED cell side (tgt_env); the candidate (i,j) set is built once and consulted per contracted tuple. Non-candidate entries are the aggregate's additive identity, exactly 0. VALUE-IDENTICAL to the dense template: a pruned pair has zero true overlap area (disjoint bounding boxes => disjoint cells), which the dense path computes as 0 and the downstream sliver filter drops anyway -- identical surviving sets, identical sums. eps is a small conservative slack (the broad phase never misses a genuine positive-area overlap for eps >= 0). PLANAR only: the envelope broad phase is a planar bounding-box test, and the narrow phase is overlap_area_planar exactly as in conservative_overlap_A_ij_planar (same src_nv / tgt_nv contract) -- the two differ only in the skeleton, conservative_overlap_pairs_gated instead of conservative_overlap_pairs.",
      "body": {
        "op": "apply_expression_template",
        "args": [],
        "name": "conservative_overlap_pairs_gated",
        "bindings": {
          "src_ring": "src_poly",
          "tgt_ring": "tgt_poly",
          "area": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "conservative_overlap_area_planar_ij",
            "bindings": {
              "src_poly": "src_poly",
              "tgt_poly": "tgt_poly",
              "src_nv": "src_nv",
              "tgt_nv": "tgt_nv"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "conservative_overlap_A_j_gated": {
      "params": [
        "A_ij",
        "src_poly",
        "tgt_poly",
        "atol"
      ],
      "description": "CANDIDATE-GATED ROW NORMALIZATION: A_j[j] = sum_i A_ij[i,j] over the CANDIDATE pairs (join.overlap{src_env:[src_poly], tgt_env:[tgt_poly]}) that survive the sliver filter A_ij > atol. THE DENOMINATOR BROAD-PHASES LIKE THE NUMERATOR: this template applies the SAME spatial-overlap join gate and the SAME filter as conservative_overlap_A_ij_gated_planar / the apply, so the surviving-overlap sets coincide and partition-of-unity sum_i W_ij = 1 stays EXACT BY CONSTRUCTION (CONFORMANCE_SPEC 5.8.3) -- gating only the numerator, or only the denominator, would break the invariant wherever a spurious sliver or a pruned pair appears on one side only. Value-identical to conservative_overlap_A_j on a gated A_ij: the pruned entries have zero overlap area and are sub-atol, so both forms sum the same surviving terms. Bind src_poly/tgt_poly to the SAME ring stacks passed to conservative_overlap_A_ij_gated_planar (the envelope broad phase reads their bounding boxes at build time).",
      "body": {
        "op": "faq",
        "semiring": "sum_product",
        "output_idx": [
          "j"
        ],
        "ranges": {
          "i": {
            "from": "src_cells"
          },
          "j": {
            "from": "tgt_cells"
          }
        },
        "join": [
          {
            "overlap": {
              "src_env": [
                "src_poly"
              ],
              "tgt_env": [
                "tgt_poly"
              ],
              "eps": 1e-09
            }
          }
        ],
        "filter": {
          "op": ">",
          "args": [
            {
              "op": "index",
              "args": [
                "A_ij",
                "i",
                "j"
              ]
            },
            "atol"
          ]
        },
        "args": [
          "A_ij",
          "src_poly",
          "tgt_poly"
        ],
        "expr": {
          "op": "index",
          "args": [
            "A_ij",
            "i",
            "j"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    "conservative_overlap_W_ij_gated": {
      "params": [
        "A_ij",
        "A_j",
        "src_poly",
        "tgt_poly",
        "atol"
      ],
      "description": "CANDIDATE-GATED NORMALIZED WEIGHTS: W_ij[i,j] = A_ij[i,j] / A_j[j] over the candidate pairs surviving the SAME spatial-overlap join gate (join.overlap{src_env:[src_poly], tgt_env:[tgt_poly]}) and SAME filter as the gated A_j (a pruned or filtered pair's weight is exactly 0, the additive identity). Bind A_j to the materialized result of conservative_overlap_A_j_gated, and src_poly/tgt_poly to the same ring stacks as the numerator. Build-once diagnostic data exactly like the dense W_ij template: the conformance runner reads it from the official build-time setup-array surface; the apply never does.",
      "body": {
        "op": "faq",
        "semiring": "sum_product",
        "output_idx": [
          "i",
          "j"
        ],
        "ranges": {
          "i": {
            "from": "src_cells"
          },
          "j": {
            "from": "tgt_cells"
          }
        },
        "join": [
          {
            "overlap": {
              "src_env": [
                "src_poly"
              ],
              "tgt_env": [
                "tgt_poly"
              ],
              "eps": 1e-09
            }
          }
        ],
        "filter": {
          "op": ">",
          "args": [
            {
              "op": "index",
              "args": [
                "A_ij",
                "i",
                "j"
              ]
            },
            "atol"
          ]
        },
        "args": [
          "A_ij",
          "A_j",
          "src_poly",
          "tgt_poly"
        ],
        "expr": {
          "op": "/",
          "args": [
            {
              "op": "index",
              "args": [
                "A_ij",
                "i",
                "j"
              ]
            },
            {
              "op": "index",
              "args": [
                "A_j",
                "j"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    "conservative_overlap_apply_gated": {
      "params": [
        "A_ij",
        "A_j",
        "F_src",
        "src_poly",
        "tgt_poly",
        "atol"
      ],
      "description": "CANDIDATE-GATED WEIGHTED-SUM APPLY (+ fold-in normalize): F_tgt[j] = sum_i A_ij[i,j]*F_src[i] / A_j[j] over the candidate pairs surviving the SAME spatial-overlap join gate (join.overlap{src_env:[src_poly], tgt_env:[tgt_poly]}) and SAME filter as the gated A_j -- the O(#overlaps) production spelling of the ESS worked fixture's equations (4)+(5), the sparse mat-vec restricted to the candidate set. Bind A_j to the materialized result of conservative_overlap_A_j_gated so the denominator is the row-sum of the same computed areas over the same surviving set: partition-of-unity exact by construction, conservation wherever the target tiles the source domain (CONFORMANCE_SPEC 5.8.3). Value-identical to conservative_overlap_apply on the same (gated) A_ij/A_j. A_ij and A_j are build-once; when F_src is build-time-known the whole apply materializes at setup (the candidate set + narrow filter select the same surviving terms as the dense apply). Bind src_poly/tgt_poly to the same ring stacks as the numerator.",
      "body": {
        "op": "faq",
        "semiring": "sum_product",
        "output_idx": [
          "j"
        ],
        "ranges": {
          "i": {
            "from": "src_cells"
          },
          "j": {
            "from": "tgt_cells"
          }
        },
        "join": [
          {
            "overlap": {
              "src_env": [
                "src_poly"
              ],
              "tgt_env": [
                "tgt_poly"
              ],
              "eps": 1e-09
            }
          }
        ],
        "filter": {
          "op": ">",
          "args": [
            {
              "op": "index",
              "args": [
                "A_ij",
                "i",
                "j"
              ]
            },
            "atol"
          ]
        },
        "args": [
          "A_ij",
          "A_j",
          "F_src",
          "src_poly",
          "tgt_poly"
        ],
        "expr": {
          "op": "/",
          "args": [
            {
              "op": "*",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "index",
                  "args": [
                    "A_ij",
                    "i",
                    "j"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "op": "index",
                  "args": [
                    "F_src",
                    "i"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "op": "index",
              "args": [
                "A_j",
                "j"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
